[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Queen's Gambit Declined"]
[Variation "Catalan Opening, Closed Variation"]
[ECO "E06"]
[Character "solid,positional"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "pawn-grab,hold-the-pawn,long-diagonal"]
[Kind "sideline"]

1. d4 d5 2. c4 e6 3. g3 { White puts the bishop on the long diagonal to press on d5 and the queenside. } 3... Nf6 4. Bg2
Be7 5. Nf3 ( 5. Nc3 O-O ) 5... O-O 6. O-O dxc4 { Now it is fine to take: White's pressure on the long diagonal is
easy to meet once the pawn on c4 is safe. } 7. Qc2 ( 7. Qa4 a6 8. Qxc4 b5 9. Qc2 Bb7 ) ( 7. Ne5 c5 ) 7... a6 { Gets ready
for ...b5, which would protect the extra pawn on c4. } 8. Qxc4 b5 { The pawn on b5 stops the queen coming back to c4
and keeps the extra pawn. } 9. Qc2 Bb7 { Black has returned the pawn on terms that suit Black: the bishop on b7 eyes the
long diagonal. } 10. Bd2 Be4 { Trades the bishop that White would use against Black's king. } 11. Qc1 Nc6 { Black has
a healthy position and can answer White's pushes with ...Rc8 or ...Bxf3. } *
